WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.186
GPU rental is useful when flexibility matters more than ownership: temporary workloads,

00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:09.424
model evaluations, bursts, distributed team access, and specialized memory requirements.

00:00:09.424 --> 00:00:13.662
Choose among major providers, specialized clouds, marketplaces, notebooks, dedicated instances,

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:17.900
and managed inference according to the control, support, interruption tolerance,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.443
and data boundary the job requires.

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:22.986
Match the device to the workload.

00:00:22.986 --> 00:00:27.224
VRAM, memory bandwidth, GPU generation, software support, context, batch, concurrency,

00:00:27.224 --> 00:00:29.767
and multimodal inputs all influence fit.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.157
Several GPUs do not automatically behave as one.

00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:39.939
Test the smallest plausible configuration with real work and scale only when measurements identify a limit.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.634
Control the complete cost.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:45.872
Include provisioning, idle time, persistent storage, caches, snapshots, data transfer,

00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:46.720
and cleanup.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.381
Use commitments for predictable demand and interruptible capacity for restartable work.

00:00:51.381 --> 00:00:53.924
Budgets, alerts, ownership tags, automatic expiration,

00:00:53.924 --> 00:00:57.315
and shutdown automation turn good intentions into controls.

00:00:57.315 --> 00:01:03.248
Build a reproducible environment, protect SSH and API access, keep secrets out of images,

00:01:03.248 --> 00:01:06.215
and classify prompts and documents before upload.

00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:10.029
Monitor service health and hardware use, checkpoint important work,

00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:12.996
and preserve a rebuild and rollback path.

00:01:12.996 --> 00:01:15.115
When the job is complete,

00:01:15.115 --> 00:01:20.625
stop or delete compute and account for every remaining disk, snapshot, log, key,

00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:21.896
and network rule.

00:01:21.896 --> 00:01:26.982
Practical compute on demand means the rental is productive while active and

00:01:26.982 --> 00:01:31.220
leaves neither uncontrolled spending nor exposed data after it ends.
